            <div xml:id="d663">

                <pb facs="0821" n="711" xml:id="pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3354: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-30T18:00:00+08:00">December 30, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 30—8:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1156. The Military Attaché at Chinchow has just telephoned that the Chinese
                    troops are now withdrawing from that area to south of the Wall, the movement to
                    be complete within this week. Margetts has been authorized by me to return at
                    his discretion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
